            <ArticleTitle>Appendicitis and malrotation.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>905-6</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A 13-year-old child was admitted with abdominal pain suggesting acute appendicitis, but with some atypical findings. A computed tomography scan showed an inflamed appendix and fecalith in the central abdomen, and malrotation. These striking images both established the diagnoses and were useful in planning the operative approach.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
